# XBD 8.2 Internationalization Variables
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Probe locale X is made with localedef and differs from the POSIX locale in
# every category (t/xloc.h), so which of the two a category follows can be
# observed. creating locales is optional (POSIX2_LOCALEDEF): these tests
# report NOTINUSE when the system does not claim it.

assertion  XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.2
class      required
since      1992
says       A non-null LC_ALL decides every category over every LC_* variable
           and over LANG.
timeout    120
test       t/001-lc-all-first.c

assertion  XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.2
class      required
since      1992
says       With LC_ALL unset or null, a non-null LC_x decides its category
           alone and over LANG, and the other categories follow LANG.
timeout    120
test       t/002-category-variable.c

assertion  XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.2
class      required
since      1992
says       LANG decides every category for which neither LC_ALL nor the
           category variable is non-null; unset and null variables are
           alike.
timeout    120
test       t/003-lang-default.c

assertion  XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.004
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.2
class      required
since      1992
says       LC_ALL naming the C or POSIX locale gives every category the
           POSIX behaviour whatever LANG and the category variables name.
timeout    120
test       t/004-lc-all-posix.c

assertion  XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.005
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.2
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       In an NLSPATH template %% is one percent sign and %t and %c are
           empty in the POSIX locale, so catopen() finds the catalog at the
           expanded pathname.
note       catalogs are made by gencat; the colon rules, %N and %L are
           tested by XSH.catopen.006 to 011.
test       t/005-nlspath-conversions.c

assertion  XBD.8.2-internationalization-variables.006
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap08.html#8.2
class      required
since      1992
says       The date utility takes its weekday name from LC_ALL, then
           LC_TIME, then LANG.
timeout    120
test       t/006-date-precedence.c
